<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>01_predatory_freelance_msa</title><style>body{font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.6;margin:40px;color:#1e293b;}h1{color:#0f172a;border-bottom:2px solid #0284c7;padding-bottom:8px;}p{margin-bottom:14px;}</style></head><body><h1>01 PREDATORY FREELANCE MSA</h1><p>MASTER SERVICES AGREEMENT (FREELANCER ENGAGEMENT)</p><p>This Master Services Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into by and between Enterprise Client Corp ("Client") and the Independent Contractor ("Contractor").</p><p>1. IP ASSIGNMENT & PERPETUAL EXCLUSIVITY:<br/>The Contractor irrevocably assigns, transfers, and conveys to Client all rights, title, and interest in and to all inventions, software source code, designs, algorithms, methodologies, and general knowledge acquired during or prior to this engagement to the Client in perpetuity across the universe without compensation beyond the base milestone invoice.</p><p>2. UNLIMITED UNILATERAL INDEMNIFICATION:<br/>The Contractor agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Client and its parent companies, affiliates, directors, and agents from and against any and all claims, liabilities, losses, damages, and legal fees arising out of any defect, bug, delay, or subjective dissatisfaction, regardless of cause or willful misconduct.</p><p>3. PAYMENT TERMS & HOLDBACKS:<br/>Invoices shall be payable Net 90 days following Client's subjective verification. Client reserves the unilateral right to withhold 30% of each invoice for 180 days as warranty escrow. Contractor waives all statutory rights to late interest fees or invoice penalties.</p><p>4. TERMINATION WITHOUT CAUSE & FORFEITURE:<br/>Client may terminate this Agreement immediately at any time without advance notice and without obligation to compensate Contractor for in-progress hours or unapproved milestones. Contractor must provide 60 days advance written notice.</p><p>5. GOVERNING LAW & JURISDICTION:<br/>This Agreement shall be governed strictly by the laws of the State of Delaware. Contractor agrees to submit exclusively to the courts of New Castle County, Delaware, bearing all travel and legal costs personally.</p></body></html>